Thanks ! Yes, lycanthropes might be difficult, but they're a lot of
fun to play, my last (non lycanthropic) characters all got quite far,
but playing the early game over and over again was getting kind of
boring, so I started a lycanthrope for a different early game, I never
expected he would make it :).

but I think lycanthropes are also greatly underestimated by many
people, lycanthropy is quite usefull in the early game, they just need
a very different playing style. The ability to summon wolves is
extremely usefull, especially winter wolfs are very strong pets in the
early game. While in wolf form you can outrun most dangerous
creatures, and let your pets do the killing. Lycanthropes also have
intrinsic regeneration, and then there is the #youpoly command: if you
get killed in wolven form you can immediately polymorph back into
wolven form (with full hitpoints!) at the cost of ten power.. These
two things make lycanthropes quite hard to YASD in the early game. You
can also easily get rid of cursed armor by polymorphing into wolf
form, which will force you to drop the items. (also as a slashem
lycanthrope you will never rip out of (uncursed or blessed) clothing,
you quickly take them of before the change.
Rogues are probably the best lycanthropes, you can collect a stack of
daggers and deal a lot of damage by throwing them (also while in
wolven form), you can also do a semi-protection run with your starting
gold. If you reach xplevel 2 you can summon wolves, which makes the
protection run quite easy (attempting it at xp level 1 is somewhat
difficult because of the lack of infravision, and you will not have
enough power for summoning) I failed to do the semi-protection run
this time because of the early succubus encounters.
As another advantage, Lycanthropes also have intrinsic level drain
resistance, which is very usefull in the late game when you start
seeing lots of wands of draining.

Ofcourse you'll need to find a way too control your lycanthropy sooner
or later or you'll get into trouble for not being able to wear armor
with magic cancellation or resistance, but you can easily do the mines
and sokoban without it. There are quite a few ways to obtain a cure
(erirefr trabpvqvat inzcverf (sbe inzcver oybbq, znxr fher lbh unir
fbzr jnl gb vafgn-xvyy gurz be gurl'yy qevax gurve cbgvbaf), n evat bs
cbylzbecu pbageby, be nzhyrg bs hapunatvat)

That said lycanthropes have a few additional disadvantages: they don't
have infravision and they can't two-weapon, and they get hungry fast
because of the regeneration (not by far as bad as vampires though) but
I think that lycanthropes certainly aren't as bad as people think they
are.

